+# Spec: Fälligkeitsdatum für Todos (Ticket #1)
+
+## Goal
+
+Todos get an optional due date (calendar date, no time) so users can see what is overdue —
+in the JSON API and in the list page.
+
+## Data model
+
+- `Todo` gains `DateOnly? DueDate` (serialized as `dueDate`, `YYYY-MM-DD` or `null`).
+- `NewTodo` gains `DateOnly? DueDate` — optional at creation.
+- `TodoPatch` gains `DateOnly? DueDate` — settable, changeable, and removable (send `null` to remove).
+- Todos without a due date remain fully valid.
+
+## Overdue definition
+
+A todo is **overdue** when it is **not done** AND its `DueDate` is **before today (UTC)**.
+A todo due today is not yet overdue.
+
+## API (`Program.cs`)
+
+- `POST /todos` accepts an optional `dueDate` (`YYYY-MM-DD`).
+- `PATCH /todos/{id}` accepts `dueDate` to set, change, or remove (`null`) it.
+- An invalid date (wrong format, e.g. `2026-02-30`, or not a date at all) is rejected with
+  HTTP 400 `{"error": "..."}` — via `ValidationException` thrown by `TodoStore`, same as
+  title validation. (Malformed JSON already maps to 400 via the existing middleware.)
+- `GET /todos?overdue=true` returns only overdue todos. Without the parameter, all todos
+  are returned as before.
+
+## List page (`Home.razor`)
+
+- Next to the title, the due date is displayed (e.g. `2026-10-20`).
+- Overdue todos are visibly marked with the word **"überfällig"** (no special styling required).
+- A control **"nur überfällige"** (toggle) filters the list to show only overdue todos.
+- New UI elements carry `data-testid` attributes: `todo-due-date`, `todo-overdue`,
+  `overdue-only-toggle`.
+
+## Conventions
+
+- TDD: failing tests first in `tests/DemoTodo.Tests/`.
+- No new NuGet packages.
+- Validation errors are `System.ComponentModel.DataAnnotations.ValidationException`,
+  thrown by `TodoStore`; `Program.cs` maps them to HTTP 400 `{"error": "..."}`.
+
+## End-to-end testing
+
+The agent tests end to end with Playwright against the running app
+(`dotnet run --project src/DemoTodo --urls http://localhost:3000`):
+create a todo with a past due date, verify the "überfällig" mark, toggle "nur überfällige",
+and verify the API filter and the 400 on an invalid date. Screenshots go outside the repo.
diff --git a/src/DemoTodo/Components/Pages/Home.razor b/src/DemoTodo/Components/Pages/Home.razor
index 10e75f0..e185a13 100644
--- a/src/DemoTodo/Components/Pages/Home.razor
+++ b/src/DemoTodo/Components/Pages/Home.razor
@@ -6,11 +6,31 @@
 
 <h1>Todos</h1>
 
+<label>
+    <input type="checkbox" data-testid="overdue-only-toggle" @bind="_overdueOnly" />
+    nur überfällige
+</label>
+
 <ul data-testid="todo-list">
-    @foreach (var todo in Store.List())
+    @foreach (var todo in VisibleTodos())
     {
         <li data-testid="todo-item">
             <span data-testid="todo-title">@todo.Title@(todo.Done ? " ✓" : "")</span>
+            @if (todo.DueDate is { } due)
+            {
+                <span data-testid="todo-due-date">@due.ToString("yyyy-MM-dd")</span>
+            }
+            @if (Store.IsOverdue(todo))
+            {
+                <span data-testid="todo-overdue">überfällig</span>
+            }
         </li>
     }
 </ul>
+
+@code {
+    private bool _overdueOnly;
+
+    private IEnumerable<Todo> VisibleTodos() =>
+        _overdueOnly ? Store.ListOverdue() : Store.List();
+}
